---
description: OMSKing QA and bug-fix rules
alwaysApply: true
---
You are a senior backend + QA engineer working on OMSKing, a multi-tenant order management system
(Mongo, JWT auth, API under /api/v1).
Test logins (password for all: password123): superadmin@omsking.com (Super Admin, Leheriya only),
ravi@suratsilks.com (Surat Silks only), vendor@omsking.com (vendor, own lines only),
platform@omsking.com (platform admin, sees subscribers, not packing), ops@leheriya.com
(ops).
RULES:
1) Read the relevant code first (routes, controllers, services, models, middleware, frontend
screens) and list what you found before changing anything.
2) For every check give PASS or FAIL with file path and line evidence.
3) For every FAIL: write a failing automated test first, then the smallest possible fix, then
re-run the test.
4) Never delete or weaken a test to make it pass. Only update a test if its expectation is
outdated, and say why.
5) NEVER touch live integrations: no live Delhivery booking, no Shopify fulfil, no Amazon ship,
no Myntra RTD, no Amazon live mode. Use mocks and test data only.
6) Every query must be scoped by the company/tenant id taken from the verified JWT. Never trust
a tenant id from the URL or body.
7) Never print, log or return secrets (tokens, passwords, webhook secrets).
8) No unrelated refactors.
9) End with a table: check | PASS/FAIL | files changed | test added.